# Supabase Configuration
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# Optional: Environment
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Optional: EAS Project ID (for push notifications)
# Get this from: eas project:info or EAS dashboard
# EXPO_PUBLIC_EAS_PROJECT_ID=your_eas_project_id

# RevenueCat Configuration (for in-app purchases)
# Get your API key from: https://app.revenuecat.com/
# Note: RevenueCat requires a development build (not Expo Go)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_API_KEY=your_revenuecat_api_key
# Optional. Overrides the built-in address of the public online-menu website
# (https://bizmanagemenu.vercel.app, see src/config/menu.ts), e.g. for a staging site. No trailing slash.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MENU_URL=

# Meta (Facebook) ads measurement. Leave both empty until you have a Meta Business account and
# an app in Meta for Developers (App ID + client token, under Settings > Basic / Advanced).
# Empty = nothing is sent and the Meta SDK is not part of the build. To switch it on:
#   1. npx expo install react-native-fbsdk-next   (the package is deliberately not installed while blank)
#   2. fill in the two values below
#   3. new native build (pod install / EAS); app.config.js adds the Meta config plugin when the id is set
# EXPO_PUBLIC_META_APP_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_META_CLIENT_TOKEN=
# Server side (Supabase secrets, not here): META_DATASET_ID and META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN let the
# RevenueCat webhook send StartTrial and Subscribe to Meta's Conversions API.
